Cancel: remove the callback at the index position. But if multiple cancelers are removed, the indices shift. Standard approach: swap with the last element and pop, and mark the canceler as invalidated. Or, set the slot to a no-op function. Safer: on cancel, set the callback at the index position to nil, and skip nils when calling. And make it idempotent: if already nil, do nothing.

```go
func (c *canceler) Cancel() {
	if c.cell.callbacks[c.index] == nil {
		return
	}
	c.cell.callbacks[c.index] = nil
}
```

And skip nils in the callback loop. This is idempotent and safe against index shifting (since we don't remove, we just nil out).

